    "totalDuration": "15 yrs 3 mos",
    "description": "Supported the EnterpriseOne offering in Oracle Cloud initiative.  Wrote BASH, Korn and Python scripts to configure Oracle Database, WebLogic and EnterpriseOne servers with new host names, ports and passwords after allocation by Cloud services.  Did the same work for previous releases of EnterpriseOne product on Oracle virtual machine environments, including ExaLogic, ExaData, Oracle Data Appliance and Oracle VM.  Responsible for compiling, maintaining and debugging EnterpriseOne software on Oracle Enterprise Linux, IBM AIX RS/6000, HPUX and Sun Solaris platforms.  Worked on projects to certify EnterpriseOne product in the UNIX/LINUX environments.  Developed, documented and executed a standardized process to certify all products with the EnterpriseOne product.  Coordinated with off-shore quality assurance team during certification projects. Performed certification of Oracle Database, UDB DB2, SqlServer, IBM HACMP, IBM AIX, HP HPUX, Solaris, Linux and numerous Oracle applications for the EnterpriseOne product.  Earned professional certification from IBM Certified Solutions Expert for DB2 UDB V7.1 Database Administration of Linux, UNIX Windows and OS/2.  Developed in-house tool to automate and reporting on user builds of the EnterpriseOne code base.  Developed the DB2 UDB content for a standard database that is used for regression and benchmark testing.  Worked with application developers and tools programmers to resolve UNIX platform issues.",
